; case: application-entry-point
; verdict: reject
; ambiguous: yes
; tests: externality=fail implementation-independence=pass non-prescription=pass
; failing-test: externality
; rationale: AMBIGUOUS, resolved REJECT. Naming the function a task runs feels like part of
;   describing the task, and it sits naturally beside the period and the deadline. It is not an
;   eADL field. §7.3 splits the task record explicitly: "eADL supplies the functional
;   requirements and constraints. The separate build manifest supplies application-code
;   associations and evidence." Test 1 settles it — an entry point states no offered feature and
;   no required behavior; it names an artifact. The consequence is concrete: with the entry point
;   in the description, the same workload cannot be built against a different implementation of
;   the same tasks, which is precisely the reuse the program exists to demonstrate.
; other-side: belongs in the engine build manifest: the logical-task-to-code association, with
;   the source or artifact identity it resolves to
;
(eadl-version eadl/1)

(defsystem app.rt
  (task sensor
    (period 10 ms)
    (deadline 10 ms)
    (priority 1)
    (entry-point "app::sensor_main")))
